# poga.local — machine-local wrapper hooks (gitignored; copy and edit).
#
# Sourced by `poga_board_ensure` at every lane launch, before the exec (WI-0028 /
# consultant B8). Repo paths and ports are machine data (P3),
# which is why this file is not tracked and this example carries a placeholder path.
#
# ── WHERE TO PUT IT (WI-0154) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   ~/.config/poga/poga.local     the MACHINE-level file — PREFER THIS
#   <repo>/poga.local             a per-member override, read second and wins
#
# Which board runs on a box, on which port, from which checkout, is a fact about the
# MACHINE, not about any one member. Read out of `<repo>/poga.local` alone it needed a
# hand-maintained copy in every checkout on the box — many of them on a busy
# machine — which is the duplicate shape `single-source-and-deliver` forbids. It is
# also why the file existed in NONE of them: nobody writes one config that many times, so
# `poga_board_ensure` was a silent no-op on the machine where every lane runs, and the
# board stayed up only because a human had started it by hand.
#
# Both files are sourced when both exist, machine-first: a member that genuinely needs
# its own board keeps the override it always had. An inherited `POGA_BOARD_CMD` in the
# environment loses to either file — a declared file is a decision, an inherited
# variable is an accident.
#
# ── POGA_BOARD_CMD ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The command that ensures the machine's board is running. Launched backgrounded, silenced,
# and never fatal: the board is an observer and must not be able to block or slow a
# lane. The board's own `--ensure` is idempotent (a matching incumbent is fronted
# silently; a mismatched one is refused toward `--restart`).
#
# On the machine that hosts the board — normally the work machine, where the lanes run:
#
#   export POGA_BOARD_CMD='cd /path/to/board && /usr/bin/python3 <board-program> --ensure <the board's own flags>'
#
# SPELL THE INTERPRETER OUT rather than leaving `python3` to PATH, and give the SAME
# flags the running board uses: `--ensure` compares its resolved repo set against the
# incumbent's, so a shorter command here is a refusal at every lane launch, and a
# different interpreter is the split-brain `--ensure` exists to prevent.
#
# On a machine that should NOT start a board (e.g. one that only reads another
# machine's board): leave POGA_BOARD_CMD unset — the hook is a no-op.
